# iOS UI Phase 2 — Production Polish

This pass upgrades the existing iOS UI architecture without changing the provider-neutral mail core.

## Implemented

- Expanded design system tokens, card styles, reusable section headers, icon badges, FAB, toast, empty state, and haptics.
- Updated the default theme to a branded violet → cobalt → cyan visual language with refined dark surfaces.
- Reworked the main tab bar to Mail / Contacts / Drafts / Settings.
- Added a privacy-first Contacts tab that merges local correspondents with optional iOS Contacts and can launch Compose with the recipient pre-filled.
- Upgraded Inbox with an overview card, richer mail cards, modern filter chips, floating compose action, refined swipe actions, empty/offline states, and snooze toast.
- Rebuilt mail detail presentation with sender/subject hierarchy, privacy banner, attachment cards, sticky reply/reply-all/forward actions, and haptics.
- Upgraded Composer with recipient chips, card-based addressing, compact visible attachment/link/schedule toolbar, gradient Send control, draft state messaging, and polished send feedback.
- Rebuilt Drafts / Scheduled Send visual hierarchy with search, summary card, status cards, swipe actions, and FAB.
- Upgraded Settings with an account hero, actionable Bento grid, connected-account entry, section headers, live theme preview, and refined visual hierarchy.
- Reworked Server Health into a status dashboard with server hero, latency/sync/capability cards, detailed connection test steps, quota, and diagnostics.
- Rebuilt legacy CloudMail Server Setup with modern self-hosted onboarding visuals and clearer security messaging.
- Reworked CloudMail Login with branded hero, card-based credentials, server selector, validation states, and haptic feedback.
- Reworked Add Account credentials / IMAP / SMTP advanced configuration into production-style cards while preserving provider preset and discovery logic.
- Added a branded bootstrap/loading state.

## Validation performed in this environment

- All Swift sources pass `swiftc -frontend -parse`.
- Package manifest parses.
- Info.plist and Xcode project parse.
- Xcode PBX source references remain aligned with all Swift files.
- Existing provider-neutral and static QA guardrails reached/pass the iOS checks available before macOS-only build validation.

## Still requires macOS / Xcode

- Full Xcode typecheck/build (SwiftUI/UIKit SDK unavailable in this Linux environment).
- iPhone Simulator visual review across supported device sizes.
- iPad split-view visual review.
- Real IMAP/SMTP/CloudMail connection testing.
- VoiceOver / Dynamic Type manual pass.
- Archive/TestFlight/App Store validation.
